  "slug": "inference-fit-6a61",
  "summary": "Eight November 2026 preprints report samplers, simulators and ML tools, plus an SKA challenge, preparing inference for LISA, Euclid, LSST and SKA data.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the construction and validation of inference infrastructure for forthcoming cosmological datasets, though not every item concerns sampler efficiency. ASPIRE reuses existing posteriors for joint dark-siren cosmological and population inference, reporting 6-28x speedups over reanalysis. samsara++ implements trans-dimensional MCMC in C++/CUDA for LISA global fits of overlapping Galactic binaries and noise. The LSST DESC cluster pipeline is validated on cosmoDC2 mocks, constraining Omega_c and sigma_8. Euclid work addresses ML components: strong-lens detection depends strongly on training-set composition, image format and ensembling, while EuclidFM learns 128-dim embeddings from Q1 photometry. SciPIC-lite offers a public HOD library for clustering observables. A differentiable GPU-accelerated 21-cm forward model targets uncertainty quantification, and SKA SDC3b finds inter-team variability among 16 EoR pipelines.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
